extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 3: England printed 40-41 (cache p041-p042, cache page = printed folio + 1). Printed 41 is glyph-corrupt in the cache (its Common items line), so the equipment, money and the Scathach heading below were read off a render; the skill list on printed 40 was read off a render too. The entry starts at The Dryad O.C.C., Master of Herb Magic heading on printed 40 and ends at Cybernetics & Bionics on printed 41, above The Scathach O.C.C. || GROUP: under The Woodland Druids (printed 38), one of its three orders; the book calls the druids practitioners of magic with a P.P.E. base, so occ_group is magic; it states no S.D.C. base, so men_of_arms is false. || XP: the column headed Herbalist, Woodland Druids, Blood Druids on the Experience Tables, printed 152 (cache p153), read off a render; a note there names the Woodland Druids as the Dryad, Filidh and Scathach. Every low bound is the previous high plus one. || POOLS: hit points not printed; P.E. + 1D6 per level as for the book''s other O.C.C.s. P.P.E. P.E. x3, +10 per level. || BONUSES: +6 vs faerie magic, foods and drinks (faerie_magic); +5 vs poisons and unwanted magic potions and foods (toxins_poisons); +2 vs all other types of magic, stored on spell_magic and ritual_magic; +1 vs horror factor. || WOMEN ONLY: printed 40 says only women are taught the dryad''s arts; the app models no sex restriction, so it is a restrictions line and not enforced. || SKILLS: each base is the catalog base plus the printed bonus. Mystic Herbology is the row of printed 22 (+20%). Identify Plants & Fruits is the catalog Identify Plants & Fruit. English has no language row and rides Language: Other at the printed figure (row ruling, 2026-11-12: no language skill rows); Gobblely has a row. The +10% to the horsemanship skill is stored as a Horsemanship category bonus beside the Pilot +5%. Hand to Hand Basic may become Expert for one other skill: costs { expert: 1 }. || EQUIPMENT: two wands, or a wand and a staff, of choice: one wand, then one more from the wands and staves together, offered from the held Millennium wand-of-* and staff-of-* rows (printed 19-22, cited to Japan) and the herb-magic wands and staves (cited to the Book of Magic); 15 of the 15+1D4 magic herbs or herb items, from every held herb-* row, the 1D4 by hand. Not stored: two wooden throwing sticks (1D6 S.D.C.; no row), scissors, a box of 50 small plastic bags, and magical bark or leaf armor (traditional, not issued). Rope or cord is stored as nylon cord; several knives as three."
