# Dryad

## Lore

The dryad (pronounced dray ad) are the masters of herb magic, healing, and the making of magic herbs, foods, wands and staves, and are said to be the most powerful of England''s woodland druids. Everything there is to know about holistic medicine, herbs, herb magic and the making of potions, powders, teas, balms and magic wooden weapons is theirs. They know far less of the wider world and other skills. Of the three orders of woodland druids, only women are taught the arts of the dryad.

## GM Notes

A kind hearted dryad often gives her teas, potions and magic for free or at low cost; most are out to help and comfort others, not to make a profit, and tend to give money away or spend it on herbs and equipment. Traditional garb is white, light tan or light green. Most wear magical bark or leaf armor from the Millennium tree or light synthetic armor. Starting kit beyond the sheet: two wooden throwing sticks (1D6 S.D.C.), scissors and a box of 50 small plastic bags.
